        "original_id": "81f05a06-9e54-595f-bb21-ec19b1ed3911",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Joseph Smith\n- Organizations: Hudson's Bay Company (HBC)\n- Places: York Factory, Saskatchewan country\n- Topics: fur-trading posts\n\nFacts:\n- In 1684, the Hudson's Bay Company established York Factory as one of its first fur-trading posts.\n- York Factory was used in the fur trade for more than 270 years.\n- In June 1765, Joseph Smith died while traveling from the Saskatchewan country to York Factory.",
